# Spec-Driven Development

This Cursor rule mirrors the `spec-driven-development` router skill — apply it when working in an SDD repo's `docs/` tree or `AGENTS.md`.

**The specification — not the code, not the prompt — is the source of truth.** Code is measured against it; when they disagree the spec wins (unless a section is explicitly *implementation-aligned*). This repo's conventions (identifier style, paths, build tool, ground-truth source) live in `docs/.sdd.yaml` — read it first.

SDD owns the **spec / document / traceability layer**; the generic engineering loop (exploring, planning, TDD, execution, generic verification, code review, branch-finishing) belongs to the **superpowers** plugin. The combined flow:

```
superpowers:brainstorming → SDD:sdd-specify → superpowers:writing-plans → executing/TDD
   → SDD:sdd-trace + superpowers:verification-before-completion → SDD:sdd-archive + superpowers:finishing-a-development-branch
```

| Intent | Route to |
|---|---|
| Explore / design an idea | superpowers `brainstorming` |
| Set up / extend the SDD structure | `/sdd-scaffold` |
| Capture a capability, write a spec, or record a decision (REQ/SPEC/ADR) | `/sdd-specify` |
| Decompose into tasks / write the plan | superpowers `writing-plans` (land it in `docs/plans/` with the SDD citing header) |
| Build / TDD / execute | superpowers `executing-plans` / `test-driven-development` |
| Tests/build pass? | superpowers `verification-before-completion` |
| Traceability / drift / spec-check / a REQ's context | `/sdd-trace` |
| Merge / PR / branch cleanup | superpowers `finishing-a-development-branch` |
| Close out the spec, index, and plan | `/sdd-archive` |

Load-bearing rules: **one canonical home** per requirement (the index links, the spec owns the prose — never duplicate normative text); **identifiers are immutable** once published; **don't mix document kinds** (no tasks in a spec, no file paths in a requirement, one decision per ADR); **don't settle open questions silently** (raise a STRAND, draft an ADR, or ask); **look domain facts up** in the named ground-truth source, never guess. Don't jump to code when no `REQ`/spec exists — explore (brainstorming) and specify (`/sdd-specify`) first. Treat superpowers' `docs/superpowers/*` design docs and plans as working artefacts: route their normative content into `docs/specifications/` via `/sdd-specify` and land plans in `docs/plans/`.
